--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -40,7 +40,27 @@ CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS items (
 - `GET  /api/health` — `{status, db}`, where `db` is `ok` or `down`.
 - `GET  /api/items` — recent items, newest first.
 - `POST /api/items` — body `{ "label": "..." }`; inserts a `source='api'` row and returns it.
+- `DELETE /api/items/{id}` — deletes the item with that id; `204` on success, `404` (`{"detail": "..."}`) if no such id exists.
 - `POST /api/chaos/crash` — hard-crash the api process (`os._exit(1)`).
 - `POST /api/chaos/error-log?n=N` — write N error lines to stderr (default `5`).
 
 Requests are logged to stdout; warnings and errors go to stderr.
+
+## Testing
+
+```sh
+uv run pytest    # runs tests/ against the DATABASE_URL Postgres
+```
+
+The tests in `tests/` are runtime tests: they drive the real FastAPI app
+in-process via `TestClient` against the Postgres named by `DATABASE_URL` (the
+same database the api and worker use in a feature env). Set it before running,
+e.g.:
+
+```sh
+DATABASE_URL=postgresql://wts_<env>:wts_<env>@localhost:<port>/wts_<env> uv run pytest
+```
+
+Every test-created row carries a per-run marker in its `label` and is removed on
+fixture teardown (see `tests/conftest.py`), so the tests are safe to run against
+the shared database without leaving garbage rows or touching live data.
